10. CHECKING STRINGS
========================================================

Python allows us to check whether a particular word
or character exists inside a string.

The "in" operator is used for this purpose.


Example:

text = "I am learning Python"

print("Python" in text)


Output:

True


Another example:

text = "I am learning Python"

print("Java" in text)


Output:

False


USING IN WITH IF:

text = "I am learning Python"

if "Python" in text:
    print("Python is present")


Output:

Python is present


USING NOT IN:

text = "I am learning Python"

print("Java" not in text)


Output:

True


REAL-WORLD EXAMPLE:

email = "niranjan@gmail.com"

if "@gmail.com" in email:
    print("Gmail account")


WHAT I UNDERSTOOD:

The "in" operator is useful for searching text
inside a string.


