11. STRING CONCATENATION
========================================================

String concatenation means joining two or more
strings together.

The + operator is used for concatenation.


Example:

first_name = "Niranjan"
last_name = "Kumar"

full_name = first_name + " " + last_name

print(full_name)


Output:

Niranjan Kumar


ANOTHER EXAMPLE:

first = "Python"
second = "Programming"

result = first + " " + second

print(result)


Output:

Python Programming


IMPORTANT:

We cannot directly concatenate a string and an integer.


Incorrect:

age = 20

print("Age: " + age)


This produces an error.


We can convert the number to a string using str().


Correct:

age = 20

print("Age: " + str(age))


Output:

Age: 20


WHAT I UNDERSTOOD:

The + operator can be used to combine strings.


========================================================
12. STRING FORMATTING
========================================================

String formatting allows us to insert variables and
values into strings.

Python provides different ways to format strings.

One of the easiest and most commonly used methods is
the f-string.


Example:

name = "Niranjan"
age = 20

print(f"My name is {name} and I am {age} years old.")


Output:

My name is Niranjan and I am 20 years old.


Variables can be placed inside curly brackets.


REAL-WORLD EXAMPLE:

product = "Laptop"
price = 50000
quantity = 2

print(f"Product: {product}")
print(f"Price: {price}")
print(f"Quantity: {quantity}")


Output:

Product: Laptop
Price: 50000
Quantity: 2


F-STRINGS WITH EXPRESSIONS:

a = 10
b = 20

print(f"The sum is {a + b}")


Output:

The sum is 30


WHAT I UNDERSTOOD:

F-strings provide a simple and readable way to
insert variables and expressions into strings.


========================================================
13. F-STRINGS
========================================================

An f-string is a formatted string that starts with
the letter f before the quotation mark.


Example:

name = "Niranjan"

print(f"Hello {name}")


Output:

Hello Niranjan


Multiple variables can also be used.


Example:

name = "Niranjan"
age = 20
city = "Bangalore"

print(f"My name is {name}, I am {age} years old and I live in {city}.")


Output:

My name is Niranjan, I am 20 years old and I live in Bangalore.


F-STRING WITH CALCULATION:

price = 1000
quantity = 3

print(f"Total price: {price * quantity}")


Output:

Total price: 3000


WHAT I UNDERSTOOD:

F-strings are useful for creating dynamic messages,
reports, receipts, and formatted output.


