14. ESCAPE CHARACTERS
========================================================

Escape characters are special characters used inside
strings.

They begin with a backslash.


NEW LINE - \n

Example:

print("Hello\nPython")


Output:

Hello
Python


TAB - \t

Example:

print("Python\tProgramming")


Output:

Python    Programming


BACKSLASH - \\

Example:

print("C:\\Users\\Niranjan")


Output:

C:\Users\Niranjan


SINGLE QUOTE - \'

Example:

print('I\'m learning Python')


Output:

I'm learning Python


DOUBLE QUOTE - \"

Example:

print("He said \"Hello\"")


Output:

He said "Hello"


OTHER COMMON ESCAPE CHARACTERS:

\n  → New line
\t  → Tab
\\  → Backslash
\'  → Single quote
\"  → Double quote
\b  → Backspace
\f  → Form feed
\r  → Carriage return


REAL-WORLD EXAMPLE:

print("Name:\tNiranjan")
print("Age:\t20")
print("City:\tBangalore")


WHAT I UNDERSTOOD:

Escape characters allow us to include special
formatting and characters inside strings.


