39. STRING IMMUTABILITY
========================================================

Strings in Python are immutable.

This means that once a string is created, its
individual characters cannot be changed directly.


Example:

name = "Python"

The following is not allowed:

name[0] = "J"


This produces an error because strings cannot be
modified character by character.


Instead, we can create a new string.


Example:

name = "Python"

name = "J" + name[1:]

print(name)


Output:

Jython


STRING METHODS ALSO RETURN A NEW STRING:


Example:

name = "python"

name.upper()

print(name)


Output:

python


The original string did not change.


To store the changed value:

name = name.upper()

print(name)


Output:

PYTHON


WHAT I UNDERSTOOD:

Strings are immutable in Python.

String methods usually return a new string instead
of changing the original string.


